# File: specs/bug-fix-pr-dependent-verification-deadlocking-delivery/feature.gherkin
#
# Generated from: specs/bug-fix-pr-dependent-verification-deadlocking-delivery/requirements.md
# Issue: #171
# Type: Defect regression

@regression @delivery-validation
Feature: PR-dependent verification deadlocks delivery
  Verification previously collapsed unavailable PR-only evidence into generic non-Pass output,
  while open-pr required Pass before it could create the PR that produces that evidence.
  Qualified local completion now enters a controlled draft, exact-SHA validation path.

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Qualified local completion emits a distinct pending readiness state
    Given the active issue scope, implementation, regression obligations, local tests, and applicable local gates pass
    And one mapped required-check result cannot exist before pull-request creation
    When verify-code records the report
    Then the machine readiness state is pr_evidence_pending
    And the exact required-check evidence is enumerated
    And the report does not claim full Pass

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Local or scope failures remain blocked
    Given a report has an incomplete task, failed acceptance criterion, stale scope, failed local test, or incomplete steering gate
    When verify-code, status, and open-pr evaluate it
    Then the report is not draft-deliverable
    And no readiness exception is inferred from Partial, Incomplete, Fail, or prose

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Only allowlisted GitHub evidence can qualify
    Given a pending-readiness marker contains evidence descriptors
    When the deterministic validator inspects the marker
    Then required_check and check_run descriptors require event pull_request plus active acceptance-criterion mappings
    And merge_blocking descriptors require active acceptance-criterion mappings and an existing pull request
    And push-capable checks, arbitrary exceptions, deferred local work, unknown kinds, and unrecognized fields fail closed

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Status distinguishes local completion from delivery validation
    Given a committed current report has valid PR-dependent readiness and no pull request exists
    When the developer runs nmg-sdlc status
    Then the stage is delivery-validation-pending
    And local verification is complete
    And PR evidence remains missing
    And the next action is nmg-sdlc open-pr for the active issue

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: Pending readiness creates only a controlled draft PR
    Given open-pr receives valid current PR-dependent readiness
    When existing delivery preparation completes successfully
    Then it creates or reuses an exact matching draft pull request
    And the draft is not review-ready or merge-ready
    And ordinary scope, version, commit, rebase, safe-push, and pushed-state gates remain satisfied

  @SCN006 @regression
  Scenario: Draft evidence is tied to the exact head SHA
    Given the controlled draft exists at head H1
    When its declared GitHub-only evidence is collected
    Then every required check records its exact name, conclusion, link, and H1
    And every declared merge-blocking observation is recorded
    And absent, stale, mismatched, failed, cancelled, unknown, or timed-out evidence fails validation

  @SCN007 @regression
  Scenario: Verification report pushes trigger a final-head recheck
    Given all declared PR-only evidence succeeds for draft head H1
    When verify-code reruns and its Pass report is committed and pushed
    Then the pull request advances to head H2
    And all required evidence is evaluated again for H2
    And H1 evidence alone cannot make H2 ready

  @SCN008 @regression
  Scenario: Fully revalidated delivery may become review-ready
    Given current issue-scoped Pass evidence exists and every required final-head check succeeds for H2
    When open-pr records the final H2 delivery evidence
    Then it writes, re-fetches, and validates exactly one final-H2 nmg-sdlc-delivery-validation marker
    And only after that marker validation succeeds may it mark the draft ready for review
    And automated-review, required-check, mergeability, CLEAN-state, explicit merge-choice, and cleanup gates remain in force

  @SCN009 @regression
  Scenario: Validation failure preserves recoverable work
    Given a draft check fails, times out, disappears, changes identity, conflicts with scope, or returns malformed evidence
    When the controlled delivery flow stops
    Then the feature branch and draft pull request remain available
    And the workflow does not emit ready, merge, checkout, branch-delete, false-Pass, or protection-mutation actions

  @SCN010 @regression
  Scenario: Deterministic fixtures preserve ordinary and fail-closed paths
    Given fixtures cover qualified PR-dependent readiness, a pre-PR-capable check, generic Partial, failed gates, stale scope, and ordinary Pass
    When the complete verification-to-delivery contract is exercised
    Then only the qualified pending fixture advances to controlled draft delivery
    And ordinary Pass follows ordinary PR delivery
    And every generic or stale failure remains blocked
